{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"087d679e636e08063ee24ae523a193d831c5eb83530e7e4d4788bba6748c3e31","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconciler JQL fetcher","key_entities":["fetcher.py","jql_active","jql_done_recent","statusCategory","status","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_paging_split.py","change 1815"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","status category","jql","active set","done set","workflow","closed status","resolved status"],"propositions":["The reconciler hardcodes status != 'Done' for active-set queries, causing closed/resolved issues in non-DIG/REB workflows to be incorrectly included in the active working set","jql_done_recent misses closed/resolved/cancelled statuses because it only selects literal status = 'Done', failing to populate the recent-done snapshot","Switching from literal status predicates to statusCategory = 'Done' / statusCategory != 'Done' makes the active/done scoping workflow-agnostic and covers all custom closed-equivalent statuses","jql_active and jql_done_recent JQL builders updated to use statusCategory predicates while preserving per-project scoping and single/multi-project fan-out behavior","Implementation verified by unit tests in test_fetch_multi_project.py, test_fetch_paging_split.py, and test_reconcile_once.py; fetcher.py size target of 650 lines maintained"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"ad49f17f-3ae1-46af-813d-cd2a5470d9b2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787897008805414897,"uuid":"a13863cc-c822-4f2e-9f2c-b7731e0bffa0"}